    </string-array>

    <string-array name="walkthrough_bodies">
        <item>A lineup manager for the TV you already have. It plays whatever this box\'s tuner scanned. It does not stream the internet and does not replace cable or DTH.</item>
        <item>Press the keys now — matching chips glow. Up/Down or CH± zap. OK shows now/next. GUIDE or MENU opens the list. Long-press BACK jumps to the last channel.</item>
        <item>Station names come from the tuner. You assign the numbers you actually remember. OK on a row makes it 1. If 1 is taken, the two channels swap. Settings can auto-renumber 1..N or reset to DTH.</item>
        <item>OK stars a favorite (filter them in the guide). Left hides a channel from the list — restore it later in Settings.</item>
        <item>Scan the QR in Settings → Phone Setup on the same Wi-Fi to reorder, renumber, hide, and tune. The server lives on this TV and stops when you close the panel.</item>
        <item>No accounts, ads, or analytics. If the list is empty, run a channel scan in the system Live TV settings first, then come back.</item>
    </string-array>
